{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Stand up, bless</b> — They instructed Israel to bless HaShem, who is from eternity to eternity, an everlasting exaltation; He is your Elohim, there is no other. The sense is: bless Him, you, and say before Him: \"Let the name of Your glory be blessed by mortals, and may it be exalted above every blessing\" — the sense being: that it be exalted after they bless You."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:26.339999135Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}